{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/657081-whats-the-horror-in-x","id":657081,"title":"Whats the Horror in X ?.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-09-08T16:01:52-07:00","id":657081,"title":"Whats the Horror in X ?.","content":"I was having this argument with some friends who hate the world of darkness. they concider that theres no real horror in the WoD, since youre the monster. Since youre already aware of the supernatural (and in some games such as werewolf) youre VERY dettached from humanity...<br /> so.. in your personal interpretation of the games of the WoD, whats the Horror element in X Game? either be mage, changeling, vampire, werewolf etc...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T16:44:44-07:00","id":657144,"title":"","content":"vampire is all about the &quot;oh fuck im eating people now and im super into it but its still bad&quot; which werewolf can have some of. actually i guess they all can. changeling has &quot;if i do my taxes this year ill die and forget about the last 6 years of my magic life&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7141-nasrudin","name":"Nasrudin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7141_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T17:14:42-07:00","id":657160,"title":"","content":"Werewolf: \u201cthe world is going to hell, and we're all gonna die!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T18:23:34-07:00","id":657250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nasrudin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/657081-whats-the-horror-in-x?p=657144#post657144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">changeling has &quot;if i do my taxes this year ill die and forget about the last 6 years of my magic life&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not if you write &quot;I'll not part with it! Not one... single... coin!&quot; on your return. Of course, that causes other problems. Also, boggans derive Glamour from hard work and jobs well done, so they might not actually suffer from it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T18:39:17-07:00","id":657265,"title":"","content":"For <b>Mage</b>, it depends a lot on the faction:<ul><li>Many among the Technocracy honestly believe in their organization's goals of reason and a utopia for humanity, by humanity. The horror there is watching that dream slowly twist, becoming a nightmare about control and power.</li> <li>For the Traditions, its watching the truth getting buried by the Technocracy. So much is possible to humanity . . .but the Technocracy's insistence of only a single truth is slowly burying all that possibility. Virtual Adepts and Sons of Ether have the added horror of watching the Technocracy misuse the science they believe in so much, and use scorched earth tactics to deny them any chance to add to the scientific paradigm.</li> <li>For the Nephandi (besides all the cosmic monstrosities), the horror comes from watching the other factions lie to the world, &quot;corrupting&quot; them. Evil is going to win, and yet the others persist in filling the heads of the others with false notions that good might triumph. So much potential wasted, so many opportunities lost. Why does humanity persist in such false beliefs, when all that matters is power?</li> </ul><br /> In <b>Wraith</b>, the horror's fairly obvious. You're trapped between life and Oblivion. You can see your loved ones, watch them suffer . . . and yet be powerless to do anything to help. You can't even hug them, or whisper a kind word in their ear. <br /> <br /> Meanwhile, what you <i>can</i> touch is just so . . . awful. Everything's is rotten and decayed, marred by the touch of Oblivion. All day, every day, Stygia rings with the screams of the unfortunates melting into soulsteel. <br /> <br /> And, always, always, in the back of your mind, your Shadow lurks . . . <br /> <br /> With <b>Changeling</b>, you know from day one that you're going to lose. Today, tomorrow, it doesn't matter. For now, you're surrounded by all the wonders ever dreamt of by humanity. Clothed in raiment spun from sunlight and frost, dining on ambrosia and elven wine (with everlasting gobstoppers for dessert!) Dancing amongst the stars, riding unicorns and slaying dragons . . .<br /> <br /> And you're going to forget any of it ever happened. Banality will rob you of even the memory of your adventures. And there's no way to prevent it. Changelings don't have the faint promise of a Golconda, Ascension, or Transcendence. You're trapped in a prison with no way out. <br /> <br /> Heading over to Asia, in <b>Kindred of the East</b>, every kuei-jin is literally damned. Rightly or wrongly, every single one of them was sent to Yomi, tormented horrifically in one of the Thousand Hells . . . And the Yama Kings, rulers of Yomi, would like to see you &quot;return home&quot;.<br /> <br /> Worse, if the kuei-jin are being honest with themselves, there's a nagging doubt that they <i>deserve </i>to be in hell. Not only do they have to feed (new kuei-jin have been known to eat people <i>alive</i> to sate their hunger), they can see the fingerprints of hell in everything they do. Its as it if they can't help but be evil . . .<br /> <br /> Even worse, not only do you have the whispers of a P'o (Shadow) to deal with, many of them can warp your very body into a horrific demonic form. And you may have to let them do so, just to survive! <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T19:35:24-07:00","id":657295,"title":"","content":"For <b>Mummy</b>, at least the first two editions, it's a sense of impotence.<br /> <br /> You are a true immortal. You <i>cannot </i>die. You possess ancient Egyptian magicks forgotten to the rest of the world. You're charged with fighting the corrupting force of Apophis/the Wyrm, and to heal the wounds left in its wake. But there's just too much evil. There's 42 of you, and an infinite number of enemies who would let the world fall into imbalance, knowingly or not. You simply cannot be in every place at once. Even if you spent every moment of your existence hunting down and foiling the minions of Apophis, for each leak you've plugged, another 50 have sprung up. <br /> <br /> Maybe you could have turned the tide back when the world was young, and in balance, but that was over 3,000 years ago. You had a shot then and you blew it. Now everyone is going to suffer for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php\" target=\"_blank\">Malkavian Madness Forum</a> - Your pbp fix. Be it nWoD, cWoD, CoC, D&amp;D or something else entirely, come over here and get your game on","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/348-infernalgoose","name":"InfernalGoose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T21:15:23-07:00","id":657365,"title":"","content":"The horror of Werewolf: the Apocalypse (to me) is that as a Garou, you are intimately aware with WHAT is destroying the world, you know that it's terminal, and you can fight the cancer that is twisting and corrupting the world you're trying to save... and you know that you cannot win.<br /> <br /> As a Garou, yes, you're removed from &quot;humanity&quot;, but the world is greater than humanity. You are a soldier. You are witness to the worst that not only Humanity can create, but the forces that make humanity terrible, and those things that pull their strings are FAR worse too. Yes, you have to do &quot;inhumane&quot; things at times because you're not human and humanity is just a part of the cog in the greater machine, they aren't the spiritual force that you fight.<br /> <br /> So, yes, while the Rage within you can be lost and you can lose yourself to it in times of stress, and your life isn't just a mindless drone in the human world (and for Lupus and Metis, you never were in the first place), you are enriched with great purpose, a destiny, and yet a doomed cause that you cannot possibly win, and yet you try. You fight. You will die.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">- Arthur &quot;Torakhan&quot; Dreese <span style=\"color:silver\"><b>David &quot;Wall-of-Text&quot; Tealdeer</b> - US2012070036\u200b - Grand Rapids, MI</span><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img855/1250/jv8k.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nmeqe3m\" target=\"_blank\">V:tM 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/pavtnjj\" target=\"_blank\">Hunters Hunted II</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/l3hjgjt\" target=\"_blank\">Anarchs Unbound</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/mxyvsy9\" target=\"_blank\">W:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/k5qe4j4\" target=\"_blank\">W20 Changing Breeds</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/m64m9o5\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3rd Edition</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/qxkop7m\" target=\"_blank\">M:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nd6kms2\" target=\"_blank\">W20BotW</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/780-torakhan","name":"Torakhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar780_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"576"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T08:19:52-07:00","id":657899,"title":"","content":"I've had this argument before, and I usually counter it with: &quot;Well, what is horror to you?&quot;<br /> <br /> Most people respond to that with examples from horror movies, which I don't think are aptly named. TERROR is more accurate for those movies. Someone or some thing jumping out and saying BOO! Something is going to hurt/maim/eat/kill the protagonists. Terror gets the heart racing. It's even in the common language. TERRORists blow up buildings, shoot people, and do things to cause fear and intimidation thru threat of violence and death. Ever notice there's no such thing as a HORRORist? Because you can't fight horror.<br /> <br /> Horror is the slow, unyielding fate. Horror means you're fucked no matter what. The original Frankenstein is horror because no matter what Victor did, as soon as he made the monster, he was fucked. Edgar Allen Poe wrote horror. Once the pendulum starts swinging or the brick wall starts going up, they're fucked.<br /> <br /> In all the WOD games, in some way, you're fucked. There is no &quot;winning&quot;, there is no escape, there is no victory but small, ultimately meaningless, ones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T10:03:33-07:00","id":658060,"title":"","content":"Concur with Papa Bear, and add in the third leg on the stool, &quot;Shock&quot;. Horror, terror and shock are related and they overlap but they aren't the same thing. I think the games were based on some kind of horror, whether they end up being played that way or not Often, the &quot;core&quot; horror conceit was even drowned out by the accretion of game materials and metaplot. <br /> <br /> For the Big Five:<br /> <br /> Vampire - It's psychological horror (loss of control, loss of consortium) with a fair dose of body horror mixed in. I've lost Vampire players in the first couple of sessions from RPing through what the Hunger feels like and, more to the point, what it's like to feed. A lot of people want to play super-sexy super-heroes with fangs. Which is fine. The game even bends that way in many ways, but it doesn't get at the core horror when it does.<br /> <br /> Werewolf - Mostly eschatological horror. The world is ending yada, yada, yada. There's no body horror. Quite the opposite. They're SUPPOSED to be that way, so they don't get body image dismorphia or the like. Werewolf is weak on the horror front Werewolves are so damn effective, one of the key elements is helplessness and they just aren't. Sure, they'll lose in the end, but that's not horror. Unless, say, you regard all of Norse mythology as a horror story. Which would be an interesting paper, but probably the finding would be &quot;not&quot;. Werewolf goes for some shock and some terror, but it's weak on those fronts too. It's the PCs who do the shocking and terrifying things a lot of the time. I guess you could say some vicariousness disconnect where the players feel horrified by the things they have their characters doing? Like I said, weak.<br /> <br /> Mage - Seems like it's supposed to be loss of mortality in the wake of godlike power. Essentially feeling your character becoming more and more numb to the world as s/he transcends. In tandem with that is the &quot;price of hubris&quot;. (I have had very few Mage games where the PCs really cared about mundane humans, particularly individually, either from the get-go or after a short span of play. So loss of companionship, being alone, isn't such a big deal. You have all that warm and cozy near omnipotence to keep yourself warm at night...) Overall, even weaker than Werewolf on the horror front. Not that you can't have horror, etc. in a Mage setting, but it can be damn hard unless it's occasional or it's something everyone's agreed on as the objective. Mages are probably the one of the least helpless PCs out there in all of gaming. Without helplessness, horror is hard.<br /> <br /> Wraith - Right in your face. You don't even get to lose the fear of death b/c you're dead. There is something even worse out there. And it LIVES INSIDE YOUR HEAD. Plus, you have the loss of companionship, aloneness and disconnection that factors in elsewhere, but magnified a lot by the barriers. A vampire CAN try to reconnect with his/her mortal life, even if nothing can be the same (ah tragedy) and/or it puts all those people in danger in several different ways. A wraith can't. There may even be a body-self-image disconnect though it doesn't get played up a ton, except through Moliate. Wraith really pushes straight in the direction of horror, but even that is not 100%. A Doomslayers game can end up looking a lot like a Werewolf game, with shock and some terror, but light on the horror.<br /> <br /> Changeling - Also right in your face on a purely psychological level. Especially the way the rules push thing. The loss of self. Knowing that, effectively, you are going to go mad, one way or another. In fact, as far as the world is already concerned, you are mad. Changelings are worse off with insanity than Call of Cthulhu investigators that are speed-reading bibliophiles. That's not the way Changeling gets presented or run very often, but, if you don't want it to be big factor, you have to make sure to deal with it somehow. We usually don't want Changeling to be horror, as we play up the horror in the other games, so we short-circuit the horror and turn the dial over to &quot;tragedy&quot; instead. <br /> <br /> So three of five can easily support horror. The other two have some potential in that direction, but it will have to be cultivated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T11:01:11-07:00","id":658170,"title":"","content":"To me Horror is in the mind. The setiing, the atmosphere, the moral dilemas, the monsters, that thing in the dark you're not quite sure what it is or what it wants but it clearly isnt a friend.<br /> <br /> The books give you ammo to fire into the minds of your players well you plant those seeds well as an ST. The uncertainty of it all, the dilemas, the drive not to fail and pleading to the gods of dice to see you through it all add up and conjure something in the mind of the player far darker and scarier than anything written on paper.<br /> <br /> To me, that's where the true Horror comes from.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7706-somuchlove","name":"Somuchlove","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7706_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T11:58:58-07:00","id":658236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/657081-whats-the-horror-in-x?p=658060#post658060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wraith - Right in your face. You don't even get to lose the fear of death b/c you're dead. There is something even worse out there. And it LIVES INSIDE YOUR HEAD. Plus, you have the loss of companionship, aloneness and disconnection that factors in elsewhere, but magnified a lot by the barriers. A vampire CAN try to reconnect with his/her mortal life, even if nothing can be the same (ah tragedy) and/or it puts all those people in danger in several different ways. A wraith can't. There may even be a body-self-image disconnect though it doesn't get played up a ton, except through Moliate. Wraith really pushes straight in the direction of horror, but even that is not 100%. A Doomslayers game can end up looking a lot like a Werewolf game, with shock and some terror, but light on the horror.</div> </div> </div> </div>To add to that: this of course depends heavily on the players and their philosophy (of all the WW lines, I think Wraith cuts the deepest as far as existentialism, nihilism, and other philosophical paths go), but being confronted by the manifest, sort-of-personified form of eternal decay is incredibly frightening. My current Doomslayers game ended with one of the PCs essentially becoming a Nephwrack priest for Oblivion as The Eternal Quiet, and she was both IC and OC very strangely OK with it. In this situation, the horror comes from seeing all the options, and arriving at the anti-natalist stance that non-existence is preferable to existence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5238-herbert_west","name":"Herbert_West","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5238_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"473"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T20:57:43-07:00","id":666422,"title":"","content":"I'll take a swing at the two splats that I'm most familiar with.<br /> <br /> Werewolf- As others have said, there's the external horror of the dying world. The inevitable slide into complete depravity and desolation.<br /> But there's also the external horror within the Garou Nation. All the best laid plans, the overtures of peace and cooperation with the other tribes. Fighting side by side with the tribes, finding ways to work together... maybe just long enough to make a difference... And then Rage takes over at just the wrong time, and all the old prejudices and suspicions start to creep back in until the entire thing explodes leaving only the ashes of lost hope. And knowing that, next time, the result will be the same damn thing.<br /> But then there's Rage itself. The internal horror. Rage isn't anger. It's more than that. It's a seething, deep-seated and ever-present hostility constantly bubbling just under the surface. Imagine the most angry you've ever been. That level of anger pales in the face of the Rage a Garou carries under his skin every moment of every day. It puts off even your own Kinfolk. They can feel it radiating off of you, see it in your eyes. And the have the scars, the miss-set bones, the battered psychology of an abuse victim that come along with the memories of their Garou-relation when they just couldn't keep it in check. Non-kin mortals... there's just not even a chance. Everything about you is hostile and wrong. They mistrust you, they avoid you, they're terrified of you, just standing near you in line to the bus is enough to make them call a cab. All this continually comes to a head, when Rage dominates and you come to your senses only in time to see the ugly aftermath of WHAT YOU ARE.You destroy everything you touch, because the Wyrm is in you, too.<br /> <br /> Changeling- I like what's been said about the loss of self, and I don't think I could improve on it. But there's an external horror to Changeling, too.<br /> The Fae are incarnations of man kind's dreams and potential. The unbounded possibility that existed when man was young. A Changeling gets to visibly and physically witness the slow death of this potential. They watch as children's natural resilience gets worn down by the monotonous grinding of the world, and those children grow into adults only to have the last wisps of glamour extinguished out of them. That childhood friend of your Pooka character, who used to share in your play as a Childling? Not only do they no longer Dream, but they are now unwitting members of the very system that's draining the world of life. And the worst part is, there's no enemy to fight. There's no existential, Lovecraftian horror to rail against in the hopes that you may one day pull through. A Changeling's fate is to spend what little time he has aware of his own nature watching everything that makes who he is... and that should have made mankind better than it is, slowly dye until he himself can't remember the loss.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7861-strafe","name":"Strafe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T04:03:28-07:00","id":666685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strafe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/657081-whats-the-horror-in-x?p=666422#post666422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Changeling-</div> </div> </div> </div>You just sold me on this <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I always viewed Changeling is a queer light, and felt it stuck out like a sore thumb. <br /> <br /> Your description makes into existential horror extraordinaire. Bravo, good sir/ma'am!<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5238-herbert_west","name":"Herbert_West","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5238_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"473"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T06:40:54-07:00","id":666936,"title":"","content":"All WW games have the horror that is the loss of innocence and wonder. In the case of Changeling and Werewolf, this is fairly literal: there is a realm of beauty and wonder and it is fading everyday.<br /> <br /> In the case of vampire, this is mainly internal: you become less and less a person who could enjoy just laughing gently and watching butterflies and hugging your family at a picnic in the sunlight.<br /> <br /> In the case of Mage, it's sort of a blend, with the world becoming less and less a place of wonder, and more about hunkering down in your grey cubicle doing a boring job full of rules.<br /> <br /> All white wolf games can be argued as being about an evil version of growing up being inevitable. Metaphorically, all WW chars face the horror of a gamer eventually having to leave his/her dice behind because the cubicle awaits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T08:02:33-07:00","id":666985,"title":"","content":"I'm going to throw in on the Werewolf front that the Horror is or can be a very palpable thing depending on how the setting is handled. Werewolves are very effective killing machines and they KNOW the truth about the world literally going to hell in the hand cart. Which can be a very good aspect of horror but often comes across as weak. A good aspect of horror as is pointed out is 'helplessness' and it's been said Werewolves lack that. I disagree. Because of the sheer amount you can throw at a pack. Find what they want to do (or thread the story seed) and then keep adding links into their activities that uncover another Wyrm threat, then add into that some Tribal politics, some inter Sept rivalries, another Wyrm threat, some unexplained connections, a risk of the Veil being breeched by people who could be so very helpful to the pack (or are even connection in a non-kin way to the pack), oh look here's a Wyrm fuelled Mundane threat that's actually been sparked by a different Pack.... and then start showing how some of these things link together, lines of cause and effect, let the heads of the hydra be peeked at with the shadows of more heads on the wall, suggested but unseen. Add into that mixing pot some connections of things that look and even act benign with an undercurrent to something far less savoury. <br /> <br /> What does the pack deal with first? Can they afford to delay tackling one obstacle in favour of another? Can they get help? What if all the other packs at the Sept are also as busy with things too? What if some of it looks insanely dangerous and yet the stronger or higher ranked garou are already fighting a far more pressing adversary? When was the last time the Ahroun slept when it wasn't a healing agg damage sleep? How many spirit bargains has the Theurge been having to make and maintain? How often does the Ragabash have to go it alone on a recon without back up because the Philodox and the Galliard are busy trying to get some back up for the main task? All of this a bit much? Imagine that backed up by RAGE? and that's before we get to character backstory plot hooks, personal RP developments etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T10:03:03-07:00","id":667136,"title":"","content":"I recall when White Wolf Magazine ran that series of articles that merged the World of Darkness and Kult, most of the lines became much bleaker as a result of the merger, whereas the particulars of Wraith changed but the tone was about the same.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T16:17:33-07:00","id":667543,"title":"","content":"There's also massive conspiracy angle to Vampire's horror. That there are ancient, inhuman creatures that are planning vast and complex power games with you and the rest of your kind as their pawns. You don't even know if your choices are truly yours. Even the Sabbat, for all their talk of freedom, might just be a tool of the Antideluvians themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my DriveThruRPG books at: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Carrie%20Kube\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....=Carrie%20Kube</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1834-yaoi-huntress-earth","name":"Yaoi Huntress Earth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T20:07:19-07:00","id":667740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herbert_West</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/657081-whats-the-horror-in-x?p=666685#post666685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You just sold me on this <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I always viewed Changeling is a queer light, and felt it stuck out like a sore thumb.<br /> <br /> Your description makes into existential horror extraordinaire. Bravo, good sir/ma'am!<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm glad you liked it. Changeling can tell some really powerful stories. But I feel like it can be a bit harder to get your head around than some of the other games. Which is why I think it's so often reduced to silliness. Which is unfortunate, because there's so much potential there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7861-strafe","name":"Strafe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}